    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on the Q4 logistics resilience report for the board. Can you run a quick analysis on our current supply chain architecture? Specifically, I need you to look at the risks associated with our current centralized intelligence model versus a more decentralized approach with localized nodes. We're looking into ways to reduce single-point-of-failure risks. Just give me a high-level overview of what that shift might look like for our efficiency and stability.",
